-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Sabre Wulf
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1984
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Sabre Wulf (1984)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         d8fb649ba5d8fa086cac43d0cd1c497e

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 conversion's colours on every figure: khaki
              Sabreman, coloured parrot, pale spider, dusky scorpion, grey
              rhino; the jungle unchanged. No white outlines or edges. The
              orchids bloom in the game's own colours, and Sabreman's helmet,
              shirt and trousers take the colour the game gives him while an
              orchid acts, as in the original. Source: Enhanced colours: from
              the Spec256 conversion (the Spectrum Magic package, credited to
              Spec256), painter not established.

  Pace        original (+1.67% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; probe 39453
              (the end of a round of the object loop: enemy pace); input keyed
              to rounds; 10 trials per scene; a fixture with the game's time
              sources read from its round counter in both runs; 1.2's Enhanced
              against 1.1's: 30 trials, -0.01 to +0.03%, 29 in lockstep
              throughout; against the original: quiet +1.61%, busy +1.72%,
              sound +1.66% (4 trials each))

  Changes     1.0: figures as Next sprites; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole
              alt ROM, so the game starts from its own BASIC; the game's speed
              restored after every hook; R kept as the original's; faster
              hooks with a frame cache; the Spec256 conversion's colours as
              the Enhanced set. 1.1: QAOP + Space option. 1.2: Enhanced
              colours: orchids show their real colours as they bloom, and
              Sabreman shows his orchid effects as in the original (reported
              by Catcher40)

  Note        Keys: any key on the loading screen, then 0 on the menu (1 or 2
              players, 3-6 controls). In play Q left, W right, E up, R down, T
              fight, SPACE pause. With QAOP + Space on (menu, off by default;
              keyboard chosen, 3): Q up, A down, O left, P right, Space fight,
              Caps Shift pause; W, E, R and T do nothing; joysticks pause on
              Caps Shift too. Every moving figure is a Next sprite in the
              game's own colours; the jungle, panel and text keep the
              original's. It starts from the tape's own BASIC, as on a 48K.
              Known issues: about 1.5 to 1.7 percent slower than the original,
              single trials up to 2.1% (the game has no frame cap to repay the
              hooks from), so enemies move a little slower. Missing: ten of
              the archive's cheats (they freeze the game, have no effect,
              misbehave or ask for a value); not reached in testing: the
              amulet by play, the cave, joysticks; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  [P1]Infinite lives
   2  [P2]Infinite lives
   3  Less enemies
   4  Always walk fast
   5  "Ghost" jungle

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

